WEB SOURCE (the specification — read end to end)
  web/src/components/forms/ComboboxMulti.tsx — the WAI-ARIA multi-select combobox primitive (a variant of
  Combobox where the value is an array; selected options render as removable chips inside the field; the input
  always represents "what to filter / add next"). Behaviour reproduced:
    - options : static array OR async loader `(query, signal) => Promise<readonly T[]>` (web `ComboboxOptions<T>`).
    - getOptionKey / getOptionLabel / getChipLabel : the three accessor closures over generic `T`.
    - defaultFilter(options, query) : trim → lowercase → label.includes(q); empty query passes all through.
    - filteredOptions : base.filter(o => !selectedKeys.has(getOptionKey(o)))  (selected rows hidden — "the user
                        never sees the same row twice").
    - visibleOptions  : filteredOptions.slice(0, maxVisibleOptions=50); the remainder → "{{count}} more — refine
                        search" footer.
    - atMax           : maxItems !== undefined && value.length >= maxItems  (options dimmed + non-interactive;
                        input placeholder → "Maximum reached"; empty `<li>` → "Maximum reached" vs "No results").
    - keyboard        : ArrowDown/Up (wrap), Home/End, Enter (add active), Escape (close), Tab (add active or
                        close), Backspace at empty input removes the trailing chip.
    - useAnnouncer    : announces the result count (No results / 1 result / {{count}} results) while open & not
                        loading, and "Removed {{label}}" after a chip removal.
    - chrome          : loading spinner (loadingProp || asyncLoading), chevron toggle (rotates when open), each
                        chip's remove button aria-label "Remove {{label}}".
  Hooks (prompt "Data sources") : useTranslation (i18n) · useAnnouncer (a11y live region) · useId (ARIA element
                        identity — handled natively by SwiftUI's own accessibility identity / focus, no explicit
                        id needed).
  Shared components used         : @/components/a11y (VisuallyHidden) — reproduced natively via SwiftUI
                        accessibility labels / traits.
  i18n keys extracted (the contract — every one promoted to the P1/S10 catalog, table "ComboboxMulti"):
    combobox.noResults "No results" · combobox.resultsCountOne "1 result" · combobox.resultsCount "{{count}}
    results" · combobox.removedChip "Removed {{label}}" · combobox.removeChip "Remove {{label}}" ·
    combobox.maxReached "Maximum reached" · combobox.loading "Loading" · combobox.closeListAria "Hide options" ·
    combobox.openListAria "Show options" · combobox.moreHidden "{{count}} more — refine search". ({{count}}/{{label}}
    expressed as %d / %@ so translators control word order.)

